From InvMove, unchanged: the icon (mixins/invmove/data/icon.png, from
common/src/main/resources/icon.png) and the English texts
(common/src/main/resources/assets/invmove/lang/en_us.json, in
mixins/invmove/config.rs). The Russian texts are this port's own
translations of them (InvMove has no Russian file).

The config screen follows Cloth Config by shedaniel
(https://github.com/shedaniel/cloth-config, LGPL-3.0), which InvMove builds its
screen with: its look is rewritten in Rust (mixins/invmove/cloth.rs), and its
arrows in mixins/invmove/cloth_sprites.rs are parts of Cloth Config's texture
(assets/cloth-config2/textures/gui/cloth_config.png), converted to rows of
pixels by tools/sprites.mjs.

This port rewrites InvMove's logic (InvMove, InvMoveConfig, VanillaModule,
ModuleImpl and its mixins) in Rust for Horizon's native mod API. Where it
differs from the original, README.md says how. It is not affiliated with
PieKing1215, Mojang or Microsoft.
